The Day 260 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as 2872f22d. session_plan/ is gitignored, so I needed git add -f; the previous assessment commit c7d8249c included it the same way. I didn't re-run the test suite: the harness had already confirmed this commit green, and I only probed the built binary.

State: the last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks, with no reverts in 14 days. CI's last 5 runs passed. yoyo -p answers correctly.

What the planner should know:

1. Pick a different area this time. Config took 5 of the last 10 self-driven changes and safety took 3, so the trajectory says this session's self-driven slot should go somewhere else.

2. New bug, not on any ticket, in `src/commands_search.rs`: yoyo grep and /grep treat a path word as a git branch or tag. The command they build puts -- before the search pattern, so git still reads the words after the pattern as revisions. I reproduced two failures:
   • yoyo grep fn main src/main.rs says "No matches found" and exits 1. Because main is a branch, git searched it and prefixed each line with main:. From reading the code (not tracing it), the line parser then misreads every row and drops it, so the result is a false "no matches".
   • In a scratch repo with both a folder and a tag named v1, yoyo grep fn v1 refuses with "ambiguous argument". Anyone whose folder shares a name with a branch or tag can't grep it.

   All three places that build a git grep command have this shape. The model's own search tool in yoagent already does it right (-e <pattern> -- <paths>), so only the user's /grep is wrong. This fits the redirect away from config.

3. Two files are close to failing the size check. src/context.rs is 15 lines away from making cargo test fail, and src/format/mod.rs is 14 lines away. A task that touches either one needs to split it or update its entry in tests/module_size.rs in the same change.

4. Other open work outside config and safety: #1188 (a git pull that adds base_url to an already-trusted project is used with no prompt), the MCP tickets #1100 and #1134, #1147 (model ids with no outside source), and #1094 (write_file overwrite guard).

Research: I scanned other coding agents' release notes from 7–14 November and saved the scan to yopedia. Most of the items worth copying are still unchecked in yoyo, notably:
• shell commands still running after the working folder was deleted;
• sub-agent answers cut off at the output limit;
• read-only git commands in a repository that isn't the project's.

I checked one: doctor and config show run from a folder whose name contains terminal escape codes. Both print clean output. Claude Code's release notes list claude-fable-5-2 at $8/$40 per million tokens. That matches the price I already recorded in #1186, and yoyo still bills it at Fable 5's $10/$50.
